From fb62d9051967530fcb34021e2776f0fac9d4eea6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blessings <noreply@example.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:01:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add staff voting with a server-enforced two-thirds rule

Staff can propose, vote FOR, AGAINST or ABSTAIN, and see aggregate results.
The database counts the votes and decides the result: approve only when FOR
reaches ceiling(eligible * 2 / 3), reject only when AGAINST does, otherwise
unresolved. Eligibility is frozen when a vote opens. Votes, results and the
hash-chained audit trail cannot be edited or deleted. Confidential matters
hide running counts and individual votes.

Additive only: new migration 0015, new screens under admin/votes, one new
button in Staff tools. No existing table, policy or screen was changed.

